| Electricity Maps as the carbon-data provider | The exact same data source Google uses for CICS; well-validated, industry-standard, low integration burden | Need for a credible, well-documented carbon-intensity signal | Strong, defensible technical choice with no changes needed | Low (API subscription/integration only) | Keep |
| CO2-avoided / Live Savings Meter tracking | Gives operators and judges a concrete, auditable ROI number tied directly to each scheduling decision | Lack of visibility into whether carbon-aware scheduling is actually paying off | Concrete, defensible proof of value | Low | Keep |

